  "heading": "\\real.cauchy.leq",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Cauchy-real order}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\real.cauchy.leq]\nDefines: leq(x_, y_) is \\total.order:on{\\real.cauchy.carrier}\nexpresses:\n. forAll: A ::= a(n_) ::= qa_ is \\cauchy.rational.sequence\n  then:\n  . forAll: B ::= b(n_) ::= qb_ is \\cauchy.rational.sequence\n    then:\n    . have: leq(\\real.cauchy.class:of{A}, \\real.cauchy.class:of{B})\n      iff:\n      . forAll: epsilon is \\rational\n        where: \\rational.zero \\:rational.less?:/ epsilon\n        then:\n        . exists: N is \\natural\n          suchThat:\n          . forAll: n is \\natural\n            where: N \\:natural.leq?:/ n\n            then:\n            . let: r is \\rational\n              where: r = b(n) \\.rational.+./ epsilon\n              then: a(n) \\:rational.leq?:/ r\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Cauchy-real order\"\n. description: \"The quotient order: $[a]\\le[b]$ when $a_n$ is eventually no more\n                than an arbitrary positive rational above $b_n$.\"\nId: \"dc1bc46f-e4ed-4968-b4f9-42abbe838ec3\"",
